  System.ELF.adam - the ELF file format's own names (elf.h), each once (AD.5a)

  The constants of the ELF64 object, executable and shared object formats
  and of the x86_64 psABI's relocations, in elf.h's own names and values
  (glibc's elf.h; every value checked against it), each in the type of the
  field it goes in: e_ident's bytes, e_type / e_machine, sh_type / sh_flags,
  the special section indices, a symbol's binding / type / visibility, the
  section group flag, the x86_64 relocation types, p_type / p_flags,
  d_tag and the dynamic flags. Adam's ELF format part (Adam.ELF.*) writes
  and reads them; a later linux runtime or tool imports them from here,
  never declaring one again. No routine, no record: the layouts are written
  byte by byte by their users. Target-neutral (an ELF file is made on any
  host), imports nothing.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit System.ELF;

public const
  /// The ELF format's `EI_NIDENT`: e_ident: its size, the magic bytes, and the values of its class, data, version and
  /// OS / ABI bytes at their indices
  EI_NIDENT: int32 = 16;
